.TH XMRIS-SDL 6
.SH NAME
xmris-sdl \- play Mr Is using SDL3
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xmris-sdl
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dig tunnels, collect cherries, and defeat monsters with your ball and falling
apples. The default controls are the arrow keys for movement and Space to
start or throw. Press F1 at the title screen to change controls and options.
Press F11 to toggle fullscreen.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-fullscreen
Start in fullscreen mode.
.TP
.BI \-scale " auto|fit|N"
Use automatic integer scaling (the default), fit the game to the window
while preserving its aspect ratio, or request an initial integer scale N.
.TP
.BI \-gardens " file"
Load a garden file. For example, use \fB\-gardens puzzle\fP to play the
installed puzzle gardens.
.TP
.B \-random
Place apples randomly among the permitted locations.
.TP
.B \-nosound
Disable the audio device.
.TP
.BR \-music ", " \-nomusic
Enable or disable background music.
.TP
.B \-help
Print command-line usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/xmris
Personal garden directory (default ~/.local/share/xmris).
Relative garden names are tried beside the including garden, or in the
current directory for the initial garden, before this directory and the
installed resources.
.TP
.I ~/.config/xmris/config
Saved preferences, shared with the X11 game. XDG_CONFIG_HOME overrides
the default configuration directory.
.TP
.I ~/.xmris.score
Personal scores.
